# Image placeholders

During the build phase, **never** import or embed real images. Use a grey placeholder `<div>` instead. Images are polished in a separate design pass.

## Rule

Every place Figma shows an image (photo, chart, illustration, icon background):

```astro
<!-- ✅ CORRECT — grey box placeholder -->
<div
  class="w-full rounded-[32px] bg-section-grey"
  style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;"
  aria-hidden="true"
/>

<!-- ❌ WRONG — do not import or embed real images yet -->
<Image src={chart} alt="…" class="w-full rounded-[32px]" />
```

- Set `aspect-ratio` to the Figma image's exact ratio (e.g. `1695 / 928`, `4 / 3`, `1 / 1`).
- Use `bg-section-grey` as the fill color (token already available).
- Add `rounded-*` to match the Figma corner radius of the image frame.
- Leave a `<!-- TODO: replace with <Image> when asset is ready -->` comment so it's easy to find later.
- Do **not** download, save, or reference image files from the Figma MCP localhost server in production code.
